  "detail": "`hasOtherApproval` accepts any latest review in state `APPROVED` from a login other than the factory's. On a public repository anyone can submit an approving review, and on a private one a read-only member can; GitHub's own required reviews count only reviewers with write access. A bot (for example `github-actions[bot]` where the repository allows Actions to approve PRs) also counts. So the gate meant to require another person's approval can be satisfied by an account with no authority over the repository. Required: count an approval only from a `User` (not a `Bot`) with push access. GraphQL `PullRequestReview` has `authorCanPushToRepository` and `author { __typename login }`; add them to `OBSERVE_QUERY` and `reviewEvidence`, treat missing fields as no approval, and also hold the entry while any such reviewer's latest review on the PR is `CHANGES_REQUESTED`. Tests: an approval from an account without push access and one from a bot don't release the entry; an outstanding change request from a push-access reviewer keeps it waiting despite another approval."
